# The built-in applications (0.0.5h): the Calculator evaluates a typed
# expression; Notes takes text and saves it with Ctrl+S (to /tmp without a
# data disk); Files lists /tmp and opens the note in Notes on a
# double-click. Windows open through the launcher search (first match +
# Enter) and are closed with Alt+F4. 1280x800.
gui: desktop up at 1280x800
cerberus kernel shell
# Calculator: (2+3)*4 = 20, shown with hex 0x14.
!mouseto 150 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.4
!key calc
!wait 0.8
!key (2+3)*4
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/apps-1.png
!keys alt f4
!wait 0.4
# Notes: type two lines, save.
!mouseto 150 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.4
!key notes
!wait 0.8
!key hello from notes
!key second line
!keys ctrl s
!wait 1
!screenshot build/apps-2.png
!keys alt f4
!wait 0.4
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key cat /tmp/notes.txt
!wait 1
hello from notes
second line
# Files: open it, go to /tmp (type the path? no: Home is /, then double-click "tmp").
!mouseto 150 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.4
!key files
!wait 1
!screenshot build/apps-3.png
# Files opens at / (frame 200,152 640x440; rows from y=229, 26 apart):
# double-click "tmp" (the 7th row), then "notes.txt" (the only row), which
# opens it in Notes; End, more text, Ctrl+S; the file has the new text.
!mouseto 260 397
!dblclick
!wait 0.6
!screenshot build/apps-4.png
!mouseto 260 241
!dblclick
!wait 0.8
!screenshot build/apps-5.png
!keys end
!key  edited
!keys ctrl s
!wait 0.8
!keys alt f4
!wait 0.4
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key cat /tmp/notes.txt
!wait 1
hello from notes edited
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
ticks=
